#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:18
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Renders a harness layer as its default interface: its left-hand nav and docs on its own theme's art, and a board of its todos and beans from which a reader reads, reviews and, when a write tool is available, proposes changes into the publication review. The theme art goes behind every docs page. Read-only is the floor. Whether the reader may write is a question about the tools the session has (git-push, github-api, github-connector) and the reader's permissions, so the gateway reads capabilities and never assumes one write path. A change a reader proposes enters the content change review in folio-assistant-core (`content-change-review.bpmn`); this process enables that review and does not replace it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:56
#. Diagram label
msgid "Resolve each harness's page ground"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:38
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reviewer"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:28
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs at site build. It composes what each layer declares and decides nothing about content."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:35
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs where the reader is, once per page. It draws and performs what the reader decided; every choice sits in the reviewer's lane."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:49
#. Diagram label
msgid "Site build starts"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The floor of the interface: everything a harness publishes can be read with no account and no tool."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The person reading the harness. Reading needs nothing; writing needs a write tool and the permission to use it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The theme art for that harness's pages, all three crops or none, and the URL scopes that make a page that harness's (`pageGround`). The site owner's ground is the fallback for a page no scope claims."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:67
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The todo board mounts inside the landing board, so harness cards and todo stickies share one surface. Each card carries an edit link only when the build composed one."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Through whichever write tool the session has. The change is a proposal: it goes into the content change review, which decides whether it is published."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn:88
